 },
 "clock": {
  "definition_used": "V4 stage_tray attempt time = sum of the planned segment durations idle -> over_din -> approach -> insert -> lift -> carry -> lower_fast -> lower_seat -> withdraw -> rise -> idle_end (gantry_ops.run_stage duration_s = sum(plan dur); qualify time_s)",
  "excludes": [
   "the 0.6 s pre-contact settle of the simulation (SETTLE_S)",
   "the 1.0 s hold after the contact phase (HOLD_S)"
  ],
  "requirement_s": 10.0,
  "what_it_measures": "the whole stage_tray operation as planned (move from idle over the docked carrier, descend, insert the fork, lift, carry 195 mm, lower and seat on the transfer-station pins, withdraw, rise and return to idle): pick + transfer + place + return, measured as the PLANNED (commanded) duration, not an observed completion time; the 1.0 s hold in which the simulation lets the seated tray settle is not counted",
  "provenance_caveat": "The original requirement text is unavailable. The earlier record attaches the 10 s target to wall time per simulated trial, while the later account uses planned stage_tray attempt time. This study uses the planned attempt-time reading; compute wall time is reported separately and is not the requirement studied."
 },
 "method_reference": {
  "citation": "T. Lipp and S. Boyd, Minimum-time speed optimisation over a fixed path, International Journal of Control 87(6), 2014, doi:10.1080/00207179.2013.875224",
  "accessed": "2026-11-18",
  "url": "https://doi.org/10.1080/00207179.2013.875224",
  "pdf_sha256": "b92e9469bd34474ac680860e606cda4518e046524bda0e04132e9529c34d2c07",
  "pdf_pages": 10,
  "redistributed": false,
  "read": "the PDF was downloaded and its text extracted (pypdf) and read; the PDF is not committed",
  "used_from_paper": [
   "section 3: dynamics R(q)u = M(q) qdd + C(q, qd) qd + d(q), control constraint sets C(q) on (qd^2, qdd, u), path q = s(theta)",
   "section 5 (eqs 22-26): change of variables a = theta_dd, b = theta_d^2, b' = 2a; objective integral b^(-1/2); convexity",
   "section 6.1.1 (eqs 27-29): a constant on each interval, exact interval time 2 dtheta / (sqrt(b_i) + sqrt(b_i+1)), handles b = 0 at the ends",
   "section 6.1.2: dynamics enforced at interval midpoints with b_mid = (b_i-1 + b_i)/2",
   "section 6.1.3: constraint sets enforced at the nodes so that speed limits bind at the nodes",
   "section 6.1.4 (eq 33): b_i - b_i-1 = 2 a_i dtheta exact under constant a",
   "section 6.1.5: the discretisation of s'' matters for fidelity (here s'' = 0 inside every segment and corners are forced stops, so no s'' discretisation arises)"
  ],
  "not_used": [
   "the paper's own log-barrier interior point method (Algorithm 6.1); a general conic solver (Clarabel) is used instead",
   "the vehicle examples of section 4"
  ],
  "derived_here": [
   "the gantry constraint sets (torque with conservative friction/damping bound, speed caps, tray non-slip)",
   "forced stops at direction-changing waypoints",
   "the exact separation into rest-to-rest groups",
   "the cone epigraph e^2 <= b, d (e_i + e_i+1) >= 1 of the exact interval time",
   "the exact continuous bang-coast-bang optimum used as a cross-check",
   "the end-point projection of the returned b"
  ]
 },
