 "limitations": [
  "Simulation only (MuJoCo rigid bodies with soft contacts); no hardware run; open-loop steppers idealised as position servos with a constant torque limit; step loss, resonance, belt stretch and backlash are not modelled.",
  "The torque limit in the simulation is speed-independent (the pull-out torque at the declared top speed); the plan keeps speed at or below 0.9 of that top speed, so the real curve's torque is at least the modelled limit there.",
  "The 10 s clock is the PLANNED duration as in V4 (not an observed completion time) and excludes the 1.0 s simulated hold; the provenance of the 10 s target is ambiguous in the record (wall time vs simulated time, see clock.provenance_caveat).",
  "Planned torque budget 0.5 of the record is a declared choice; the measured peaks include the position-loop transient of the bang-coast-bang law and are reported per phase.",
  "The tray non-slip constraint uses mu_min = 0.3 with a safety factor 2; it is conservative for the Y carry only (the only horizontal motion while the tray is carried); seating on the pins and insertion contacts are not constrained by the formulation and are judged only by the forward simulation.",
  "Plant margins (+5 % inertia and damping, +10 % friction) cover the declared extra perturbation range; the confirmatory draws stay inside it.",
  "Variants A and B of one seed share one disturbance draw; they are analysed as clusters.",
  "The path is fixed (the V4 nominal waypoints); a different path or a non-stop corner blend could be faster and is not studied.",
  "Mechanical positive work (work_J) is a proxy, not electrical energy or efficiency; driver and motor losses are not modelled.",
  "Unmodelled hardware items of V4 remain: Z holding when unpowered, driver temperature in the closed box, belt efficiency, LM8UU load rating.",
  "The V4 runner stitches three phases: the contact phase starts from the free-air end position with zero velocity, and the final free-air phase starts at the commanded withdraw pose; this applies to both arms (residual lag at those boundaries is at most about 0.01 mm on Z for the optimised law).",
  "The clock ends when the reference ends: the optimised law leaves 0.24 to 0.30 mm of Y lag at the end of idle_end, which settles to 0.05 mm within 0.035 to 0.066 s (supplementary check, outside the frozen protocol); the baseline leaves under 0.02 mm.",
  "This confirmatory cohort (new seeds 9100..9149 plus the declared extra plant perturbation) is a distinct cohort from the V4 qualification (seeds 1000..1029, 20/30 and 22/30); its baseline success (27/50 A, 32/50 B) is not a re-measurement of the V4 rate.",
  "The failure mechanism in both arms is dominantly tray_not_seated (the fork's capture of the dock error, a geometric limit documented in V4); the time law does not address it.",
  "Solver accuracy: Clarabel tolerances 1e-8; computed times carry solver-level error of about 1e-5 relative; ECOS cross-check status often 'optimal_inaccurate' (recorded)."
 ],
